SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DRC: One year on, 'State of Siege' used as a tool to crush dissent","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-05-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/05/drc-one-year-on-state-of-siege/","claim":"Amnesty said the state of siege in North Kivu and Ituri was being used to crush dissent, with two activists killed by security forces and dozens of critics arbitrarily detained on trumped-up charges.","locator":"lines 64-70, 79-94","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous briefing with named victims, dates, and a direct description of emergency-rule abuse.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within the 2022 target period; the state of siege began in 2021 but remained active throughout 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct for the emergency regime; the abuses were carried out by security forces operating under a measure Tshisekedi kept in force and extended.","contrary_evidence":["The government said the state of siege aimed to protect civilians from armed groups.","Armed-group violence also continued in the affected provinces."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.5","4B.8","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DRC: Stop using prolonged state of siege as excuse to crush protests","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/09/drc-stop-using-prolonged-state-of-siege-as-excuse-to-crush-protests/","claim":"Amnesty said authorities threatened to crush protests in North Kivu, that critics of the state of siege had been arbitrarily detained and sometimes prosecuted by military courts, and that Tshisekedi needed to lift blanket protest bans to protect civic space.","locator":"lines 61-78","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights briefing focused on protest suppression, arrests, and civic-space restrictions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Strong state nexus through the president-declared state of siege and the military/police authorities appointed and accountable to him.","contrary_evidence":["The protests were also directed at M23 and MONUSCO, not only at the presidency.","The government framed the state of siege as a security measure."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.5","4B.8","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Félix Tshisekedi modifie l’ordonnance sur l’état de siège et réduit les compétences pénales accordées aux juridictions militaires","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/03/25/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-modifie-lordonnance-sur-letat-de-siege-et-reduit-les-competences","claim":"Tshisekedi signed an ordinance changing the state-of-siege rules so military courts handled only specified grave offenses, reducing the prior transfer of civilian criminal jurisdiction to military courts.","locator":"lines 105-128","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a presidential ordinance with the text and stated government rationale summarized in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential action, and a partial corrective response to criticism of the original emergency regime.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying state of siege remained in force.","The reform did not end the broader militarization of civilian justice."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.5","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Félix Tshisekedi s’engage à accompagner la Dépénalisation des délits de presse et à Garantir l’indépendance des médias","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-02-01","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/02/01/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-sengage-accompagner-la-depenalisation-des-delits-de-presse-et","claim":"At the close of the media states-general, Tshisekedi said he would accompany decriminalization of press offenses and guarantee media independence, while a committee would follow up implementation.","locator":"lines 102-110","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of the president's own statement and the reform package presented to him.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential statement, with some uncertainty because it was a commitment rather than completed reform.","contrary_evidence":["The same media environment still featured arrests and pressure on journalists in 2022.","The article describes promised reforms, not yet completed changes."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.6","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: le gouvernement adopte le texte modifiant la loi sur l’exercice de la liberté de la presse","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-10-15","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/10/15/rdc-le-gouvernement-adopte-le-texte-modifiant-la-loi-sur-lexercice-de-la-liberte-de-la","claim":"The government adopted a bill modifying the 1996 press law so it would cover freedom of information, online media, and public-service independence more explicitly.","locator":"lines 121-127","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous reporting of a concrete legislative reform package adopted by the cabinet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Partial but meaningful: this was a government action under Tshisekedi's presidency, though the article does not isolate his personal initiative.","contrary_evidence":["Implementation still depended on parliamentary passage and later practice.","The same period also saw continuing press arrests and pressure."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.6","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : au regard des dérapages constatés sur les réseaux sociaux, Félix Tshisekedi demande au gouvernement de finaliser le projet du Code du Numérique","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-02-20","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/02/20/rdc-au-regard-des-derapages-constates-sur-les-reseaux-sociaux-felix-tshisekedi-demande","claim":"Tshisekedi asked the government to finalize the Digital Code, describing the need for a repressive device adapted to cybercrime and warning media and other actors to respect the law.","locator":"lines 105-109","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a council-of-ministers communication and the president's framing of digital regulation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential direction on digital controls and cybercrime regulation.","contrary_evidence":["The article frames the measure as a response to cyberharassment and tribalist content, not purely political censorship.","The text reports a proposal/finalization push rather than a fully enacted law."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Provincial elections a dress rehearsal for 2023 polls","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-05-10","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/5/10/dr-congo","claim":"Al Jazeera reported that the May 2022 gubernatorial elections were tainted by irregularities, including allegations that candidates were bribed and provincial MPs were paid to vote in ways that favored the ruling coalition.","locator":"lines 97-105, 121-125","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent reporting with on-the-record civil-society and analyst allegations tied to a specific 2022 election process.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Partial but meaningful: the elections were run under Tshisekedi's presidency and the irregularities were attributed to the ruling coalition and its control over the process.","contrary_evidence":["The article also notes some women were elected and that some seats were competitive.","It does not prove a direct presidential order for each alleged bribe."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Denis Kadima et le bureau de la CENI, victimes du péché originel ?","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-09-04","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/09/04/rdc-denis-kadima-et-le-bureau-de-la-ceni-victimes-du-peche-originel","claim":"A GEC/Ebuteli/BERCI survey found only 39 percent of Congolese respondents trusted the CENI to organize credible, free, and transparent elections, and the article says the lack of consensus and opacity in the CENI appointment process reinforced suspicion.","locator":"lines 98-104","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reports on a named survey by recognized research organizations and gives the key trust metric and explanatory interpretation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and focused on the pre-2023 electoral environment.","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the result reflects the appointment design and operating environment Tshisekedi helped shape through CENI selection.","contrary_evidence":["It is a survey of trust, not a direct finding of fraud.","The article credits Denis Kadima with technical expertise."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC-CENI : Félix Tshisekedi a investi les trois membres de l'opposition","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-01-07","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/01/07/rdc-ceni-felix-tshisekedi-investi-les-trois-membres-de-lopposition","claim":"Tshisekedi formally invested the three opposition delegates to the CENI after their approval by the National Assembly, completing the commission's membership.","locator":"lines 103-107","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting of a dated presidential act and the composition of the electoral commission.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential action that included opposition representation, though the surrounding CENI design remained contested.","contrary_evidence":["Opposition parties still disputed whether the CENI was genuinely independent.","The commission's broader composition remained politically contested."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Treatment by authorities of political opponents, including those who are members of the UDPS or the FCC (2020-March 2022)","publisher":"Immigration and Refugee Board of Canada via ecoi.net","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2072293.html","claim":"The IRB summary says that in January 2022 FCC protests in Haut-Katanga were repressed by police, while a UDPS march the same day proceeded without police intervention, showing uneven treatment of opposition-aligned political activity.","locator":"lines 65-66","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Government research response compiling multiple contemporaneous sources and specific 2022 incidents.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers January 2022, within the target period.","ruler_attribution":"Partial but meaningful: the unequal policing of opposition activity occurred under Tshisekedi's administration and reflects tolerated partisan enforcement.","contrary_evidence":["The source is a research summary rather than a single primary document.","It does not prove a presidential order for the police response."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.5","4B.7","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Treatment by authorities of political opponents, including those who are members of the UDPS or the FCC (2020-March 2022)","publisher":"Immigration and Refugee Board of Canada via ecoi.net","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2072293.html","claim":"The IRB summary reports that FCC lawmaker Josue Mufula was arrested and detained for criticizing the extension of the state of siege and was released the next day.","locator":"lines 67-68","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Government research response summarizing a specific 2022 arrest with named actor and context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target period.","ruler_attribution":"Partial but meaningful: the arrest was by state authorities operating under the ruler's emergency framework, though the arresting chain is not fully spelled out.","contrary_evidence":["He was released the next day, suggesting some remedial action.","The source does not establish a direct presidential order."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo names new army chief among broad military reforms","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/05/congo-security","claim":"Reuters reported that Tshisekedi replaced the head of the armed forces as part of military reforms and that almost the entire staff was replaced by young officers, several from the Republican Guard.","locator":"lines 668-677","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-sourced report on concrete personnel changes and the government's own explanation of the reform.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential appointment power, with some ambiguity because the government framed the change as reform for efficiency.","contrary_evidence":["The government said the change aimed at boosting efficiency and military professionalism.","This is more about military control than civil political pluralism."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.5","4B.10"]}

